  "result": "I've successfully created the overdue report module with comprehensive tests. Here's what was implemented:\n\n**`src/reports.js`**\n- `overdueInvoices(invoices, asOf)` function that:\n  - Filters invoices with status 'issued' or 'partially_paid'\n  - Excludes invoices where dueDate >= asOf\n  - Returns array of objects: `{ number, customerId, dueDate, daysOverdue, due }`\n  - Calculates `daysOverdue` as the number of days between dueDate and asOf\n  - Calculates `due` using `invoiceTotals` to account for VAT, discounts, and vouchers\n  - Sorts by `daysOverdue` descending (most overdue first)\n\n**`test/reports.test.js`** - 23 comprehensive tests covering:\n- Empty invoices and no overdue cases\n- Status filtering (includes issued/partially_paid, excludes draft/paid)\n- Correct daysOverdue calculation\n- Due amount calculations with VAT, discounts, and vouchers\n- Sorting by daysOverdue\n- Edge cases like exactly on due date (not overdue), single day overdue, many days overdue\n- Multiple lines and different customer IDs\n- Immutability of input\n\n**Test results:** All 255 tests pass (including the 23 new tests).\n\nThe implementation is ready to commit. Would you like me to proceed with committing these changes to git?",
